  "ref": "LUK.6.45",
  "review_notes": [
    "Corrected s018: the supplied *treasure* now rides with the article under rule 102 and the `added` unit is dropped, so the verse's two identical article-plus-substantival-adjective phrases — ὁ πονηρός → *the evil man* and τοῦ πονηροῦ → *the evil treasure* — are analysed alike, as rule 24 requires and as LUK.6.23, LUK.6.26 and LUK.6.30 already do in this chapter.",
    "Rule 103 does not reach either phrase: its reason is that the token licensing the supplied English is already spent, and here the licensing token is the article, whose own English realization the nominal is under rules 22, 49 and 102. Reading either as a rule 103 repetition remains defensible, but not one of them and not the other."
  ]
